what is up everybody this is kevin  johnson from the community team here at  blizzard entertainment today we have a  real treat for you as will be taking a  first look inside the heroes of the  storm alpha please keep in mind that  this is a very early build of the game  and as such is a work in progress much  of what you see here will be changing as  the game develops well there's a lot to  get to so let's jump in as soon as you  boot up into the game you're immediately  taken to a tutorial that walks you  through the basics the tutorial will  give you all the info you need to get  started playing from character movement  to intro tactics and don't worry Luther  isn't really gonna sound like that thank  the light another hero when you finish  the tutorial you'll unlock quests quests  are specific challenges that grant  experience points are XP when you  complete them daily quests unlock each  day offering new challenges across the  game we even offer quests unique to each  hero that help you unlock additional  skin variations not only do quests grant  you XP but some quests even unlock  additional modes and features when you  complete them alright so continuing  through the UI prompts will bring you to  the game's current home screen one of  the first things you will notice is the  visual progression of your account level  shown at the bottom of the screen this  will give you a quick snapshot of where  you currently sit in a leveling  experience and provide goals to shoot  for in order to unlock various game  features in the top right hand corner of  the screen you'll find your quest log  this is where you'll find your active  quests that we described earlier your  menu where you'll find options related  to gameplay graphics sound and more is  also located here in the lower right  hand corner of the screen or the game's  current social features the far right is  your friends list you can add friends to  your list by either using their account  email address or their Blizzard  battletag next to your friends list is  the party tab Heroes is a game that  really shines when you're playing with  friends or people you've met using the  game's matchmaker this window is the  place to kick off a party from your  friends list or add new members to fill  one out up at the top of the screen  you'll find the watch tab while this  menu is not yet available we are looking  to support some of the awesome replay  features currently found  starcraft 2 along with some fancy new  ones as we get further in development  now let's jump into a game if you click  on the play tab at the top of the screen  you'll be brought to a screen that gives  you a variety of different game modes  practice cooperative and vs let's start  with practice mode practice mode pits  you in for computer-controlled allies  against a full team of  computer-controlled enemies this is a  great mode to start off on and gives you  the full heroes experience without the  added pressure of playing against other  people this is the hero select screen  you can select from available heroes at  the top of the screen simply click on a  desired heroes portrait or choose the  question mark on the left to queue up as  random the heroes that are available to  you our heroes you have purchased along  with heroes that are currently part of  our ongoing free hero rotations we'll  talk more about that later clicking on  the hero details in the lower left  corner of the screen will bring up a  variety of specifics about your hero  this green will be changing quite a bit  but the game's development for now you  can view your heroes abilities their  various mounts skins and skin variations  every skin that you purchase will have  skin variations that change the color of  that skin you unlock the ability to  access these variations by completing  quests specific to each hero when you  have your hero selected and you're ready  to do battle hit the ready button to get  started once you complete your first  practice match you'll be awarded  experience for your efforts and you'll  unlock cooperative mode cooperative mode  pits you in for other live players  against the team of AI opponents this  mode will introduce you to playing with  live teammates and further prepare you  for play against a team of real  opponents if you want you can directly  invite players to your party from here  by clicking on the purple invite buttons  you see on the screen if you don't have  a friends list to pull from no worries  cooperative mode is designed to match  you with equally skilled allies using  the game's matchmaker Valley Road will  even be working to line up the AI  difficulty to match your team's level of  skill the hero you selected is the hero  you will play in game with others you  choose who you want to play before you  ever start queuing whenever you finish a  game with live allies you'll have an  option after the game to invite players  you enjoyed playing with to join your  party  this feature can help you find skilled  players you can formally party with not  just for your next game but possibly  others in the future okay so now you've  unlocked versus as you might expect  versus is where we put you and for the  live players into battle with other  player teams here you have all the same  options as before check out heroes  invite friends or dive into a game it is  important to note however that while  ranked mode will eventually be coming  for vs play it is not yet implemented  next let's take a quick look at the shop  where you can check out heroes skins and  mounts by default you brought to the  hero shop where you can click on the  left and right arrows to browse heroes  available for purchase or navigate using  these Rock and hexagons if you want  there is also a search option that lets  you browse heroes by their franchise  hero named hero role and hero title you  can also sort all of the heroes  alphabetically by their release date or  by price throughout the life of the game  we will be offering different groups of  heroes that you will be able to try free  of charge for a limited time we call  this our hero rotation and all heroes in  the current rotation are marked with an  icon so you can easily spot them when  you click on a hero you will be taken to  that heroes page you can easily see the  hero's name what their awesome title is  which Blizzard franchise they represent  and all abilities a hero can perform you  can also spend your hero around to check  out their model in fact the model you  see here is exactly the same model used  in game if you want to test a hero and  their abilities before you purchase it  click on the try button at the bottom of  the heroes page this takes you to a  sandbox map where you have complete  control over millions spawning objective  control and ability cooldowns we think  it's important that you have a chance to  try out a hero in battle before making a  commitment to purchase once you've tried  a hero and are interested there are  options to purchase a hero using your  in-game gold or your battlenet balance  you can purchase heroes right away in  the cell phone while there will be  periodic account wipes as we progress  through testing anything you purchase  real money will be refunded to your  battlenet balance after a wipe if you  click on the appearance tab you can  check out all the skins and skin  variations available for your hero  finally you'll notice the talents tab  this page is definitely a work in  progress so expect a great deal more in  the future for now you can view the  leveling progression of your heroes  abilities here when shopping for skins  you have many of the same sorting  choices available to you as when  shopping for heroes you can search by  either the hero name or the skin name  you can also sort by all hero skins or  just skins for heroes that you own  clicking this drop-down menu lets you  sort skins in alphabetical order by  release date or by price just like our  heroes the skins you see are the exact  models available in game here you can  browse the different variations for a  skin if you're interested you can  purchase it down at the bottom of the  page finally you can also browse mounts  that are available for purchase under  the mounts tab alright folks that pretty  much wraps us up for this walkthrough we  are extremely excited to begin testing  this game publicly and look forward to  slowly but surely opening our doors to  increasing numbers of testers keep in  mind again everything you have seen here  is in an early alpha state and will most  likely change and evolve with time we  have additional features and technology  to bring to the table what you see here  is simply a starting point to support  the testing of our online infrastructure  stay tuned to heroes of the storm calm  for more information on our testing  plans and if you would like to be  considered for participation in this  alpha or our future beta tests be sure  to opt in via the links on our website  I'm Kevin Johnson for Blizzard  Entertainment we'll see you next time  you

